WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Separate the listening level from the teaching approach.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:09.440
Analytic training works from smaller speech components, such as vowel and consonant contrasts.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.170
The course calls this bottom-up.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:19.110
Synthetic training uses meaningful speech, grammar, and context to support sentence perception and conversation.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.750
That is the top-down approach.

00:00:22.195 --> 00:00:27.315
Pragmatic training helps the listener control communication variables and repair breakdowns.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:37.760
Moving closer, improving the signal-to-noise ratio, establishing the topic, or asking a specific clarification can help recover a missed message.

00:00:38.275 --> 00:00:42.275
The aim is to recognize the problem and choose a useful action.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.030
Eclectic training combines strategies for the individual child.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:54.600
A session might refine a vowel contrast, use it in a meaningful sentence, and practice requesting clarification.

00:00:55.425 --> 00:00:58.065
Identification tells you what the response requires.

00:00:58.595 --> 00:01:02.435
Analytic or synthetic tells you how the training is organized.

00:01:03.015 --> 00:01:07.095
Neither label replaces assessment of the child's access and needs.

